{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1549589-custom-courts","id":1549589,"title":"Custom Courts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-27T00:23:55-07:00","id":1549589,"title":"Custom Courts","content":"Been designing my local area with my IRL group for fun and use in the future, we decided to do custom courts for the area, so we brainstormed ideas. I took our brainstormed ideas and wrote out how they might be represented. There are 4 Courts<b>, </b>the Court of Stone, the Court of Leaves, the Court of Soot, and the Court of Rain.<br /> <br /> I would love and appreciate and potential feedback, criticism or otherwise!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PRVpSd3DFng_wRz3hVPjF5V3QWA6nMZPl1BMbes5ons/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PRVpSd3DFng_wRz3hVPjF5V3QWA6nMZPl1BMbes5ons/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PRVpSd3DFng_wRz3hVPjF5V3QWA6nMZPl1BMbes5ons/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PRVpSd3DFng_wRz3hVPjF5V3QWA6nMZPl1BMbes5ons/edit?usp=drivesdk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","user":"Rexitonic","date":". 04-21-2025, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-27T14:08:59-07:00","id":1549599,"title":"","content":"Seeing if I've properly understood the cycle, because it's a bit abstract:<br /> <br /> The Court of Leaves takes over from the Court of Stone when it's time to focus on innovation, investigation, and other greater than normal levels of activity.<br /> <br /> The Court of Soot takes over from the Court of Leaves when the novelty dies down and it comes time to winnow down the elements of the previous baseline.<br /> <br /> The Court of Rain takes over from the Court of Soot once the necessary supports for the new material are laid down and there's no more old material slated for retirement.<br /> <br /> And the Court of Stone takes over from the Court of Rain once the new baseline has been massaged into a stable configuration.<br /> <br /> Is that right? Does the overall structure of the freehold itself change with each cycle? Is this a long-term shifting or is it as chaotic as would be implied by doing so on the same timescale as the Seasonal Courts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-27T14:52:43-07:00","id":1549606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1549589-custom-courts?p=1549599#post1549599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that right? Does the overall structure of the freehold itself change with each cycle? Is this a long-term shifting or is it as chaotic as would be implied by doing so on the same timescale as the Seasonal Courts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is the current cycle of the Courts, these are all first drafts however, so things are warrant to change, hence why I wanted to post and ask for feedback. At some point in the relative future, I'm gonna go back over and add or change things I imagine.<br /> As for the other two questions, in the current, most basic form of the imagined system, the overall structure isn't changed too much, however I'm gonna read some other books to get a better grip on these things, I'm going off of second edition and wanna reread them, and see what 1e could offer in adding depth.<br /> Again, the current system is going off of the seasonal structure, though, I'm personally thinking I'm gonna have them stray away from that, but I need to establish what that could possibly be. How do they recognize it is time to switch? I wrote the Court of Rain on being the ones to push for the change, especially if it takes too long, however again, I need to establish how and when they switch otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-27T18:31:06-07:00","id":1549612,"title":"","content":"Bearing in mind the nature of early drafts, further notes:<br /> <br /> Something I would note to be cautious of is that, for want of a better term, the Courts seem to be leaning a bit far into niches that are more generalized aspects of a working freehold \u2014 change over time is going to happen regardless of which Courts a freehold has by virtue of the simple fact that it exists as a part of the world and is made up of people, whereas pretty much <i>every</i> Court is a collection of rituals and traditions and cyclic activity and members building new lives divorced from their old ones, with the details of its original Bargain lost to time and psychic feedback. The Courts of Soot and Rain also feel a bit fuzzy when one is described as focusing on getting rid of old things to make way for the new and the other is described as making sure cycles continue to turn \u2014 it may be wise to take steps to either make this a three-Court freehold or better differentiate the two beyond their general demeanor.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with having a Court structure that goes in a straightforward cycle whose Courts specialize more toward one common focus over the others, of course, but unless the freehold is very geographically limited it's probably going to have a lot of different placements along the cycle that the Courts could conceivably point to as a mark of their appointed time to rule; given that the Courts' patrons as currently described are the Rocky Mountains and three mystery figures and the simplest cyclic Court structures are those tied to beings and phenomena whose interrelation is easy to understand, it may be wise to either figure out (at least what the freehold believes) the relationship is between their patrons or shift to a more deliberate and arcane system of ceding power built on whatever circumstances led these forces to all patronize changelings who belong to this freehold.<br /> <br /> I'll also add that the ability of a Court's patron to be mysterious is somewhat limited by the nature of Court Contracts \u2014 their identity and changelings' emulation of its qualities is the literal basis for the powers they grant to the Lost through the Wyrd, so even if all the modern adherents to a Court were inducted by another member they can figure pretty easily that, say, a Court whose members all start to grow red fur and produce cold fire and develop uncanny wit probably has something to do with the mythical kitsune, especially if they live in a place where such a being is part of the cultural context (however esoterically).<br /> <br /> Are the non-Stone patrons intended to all be discrete powerful beings rather than aspects of the world personified through their engagement with the fae perspective like the seasons, or are there stories of ancient monsters using the freehold to uphold a mutual agreement with the land? Does the Underworld have anything to do with this (e.g. is there something to do with a River that's particularly accessible from the Rockies)? Are any of the patrons related to that fallen giant? There obviously don't have to be hard answers yet this early in the process, but it's worth thinking about what the local changelings say about their cultural touchstones when dealing with one of the anchoring elements of a splat whose signature struggle is with keeping their story straight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-27T22:46:32-07:00","id":1549613,"title":"","content":"I love this feedback so much, thank you! Anyhow, first thing first:<br /> <br /> - I was definitely overly anxious when writing these when it came to writing these Courts, I was worried of making them too ambivalent or purposeless, and ended up diving into niches, I'll definitely be working on broadening and generalizing them in the future. As for the last point in that, about the Courts of Rain and Soot, I'll look into, right now I don't have any ideas for further separating them, but it is something I'll think on.<br /> <br /> - Sounds like the next biggest problem I'm going to focus on, though, are the Patrons. When writing the Court of Stone, I came up with the Rocky Mountains as a Patron and thought it was an awesome idea that could work really well, however when it came to writing the others I felt overshadowed by that and wasn't really sure where to push them in terms of Patronage, so I wrote in essentially cool placeholders. I'm thinking I want to keep the Court of Leaves Patron a secret either way, as it seemed in line with my imagination of them. Which would lead to the two courts that are currently conflicting, perhaps figuring out their patrons would assist in this? Maybe the Crying Lady (A placeholder name at the moment), is a powerful ghost or Kerberoi, or something connected to the Underworld, them coming in after the Court of Soot leaving them in the death of the grief that Soot holds dear? That would still be awfully specific, however. Or perhaps all the Patrons are all instead aspects of the fallen giant.<br /> <br /> - I'm not too sure how I want to handle the cycles to be honest, I'll talk to my group about that in the meantime.<br /> <br /> Again, I really appreciate the feedback, it's exactly what I was looking for! Hopefully I can get these situated more and get back to crafting them soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T00:59:20-07:00","id":1550205,"title":"","content":"Finished the Court of Stone second draft a while ago, though I regrettably took sleeping pills midway through and lost my path, so some bits are a bit spotty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b> The Court of Stone say, that after their Durance, things can\u2019t ever really change again, not really, not in any way that matters, best to bunker down and reinforce what's already here, and work away their worries and trauma. The liquid whims of their captors were difficult to manage, their magics hard to grasp, at least that was in Arcadia, their escape, through the Thorns, through their memories, back Ironside, the last real change, it allowed them to turn the Wyrd into concrete and rebar. Now they toil away at the literal and metaphorical walls and architecture, at the infrastructure, the beating heart of the freehold, finding idealistic ritual and confidence in the real world's comparative predictability, trying their best to support and find places in the lives of those like they once were, despite knowing they\u2019ll never return to such predictable, monotonous bliss.<br /> The Slate Circle finds pride in their reliability, even if they\u2019re not the best at something, they\u2019ll see it through, if you need someone to be there and listen, a Granite courtier is your best bet. They\u2019re not the most social court though, while they\u2019re not dull enough to completely cut themselves off, you\u2019re most likely to find them isolated to just small numbers or even singular individuals, working on solo projects, connecting with predictability of the world such as through sciences or cooking, or doing as many various jobs they can find. They work and toil, but they\u2019re not slaves, not anymore at least, and always demand payment of some kind, favors, money, exchange, whatever it is, they always expect remittance.<br /> When in power the Court focuses on reinforcing and supporting the other courts, focusing less on themselves and giving breathing room to the others, when out of power is when they focus most on themselves, ensuring their lives are steady, their projects are healthy, and the portals to the hedge secure.<br /> Following their escape from Arcadia, a small motley quickly formed, with the goal of finding a Patron, one of them worked slow and steady, researching proper recourse and mental preparations, another treading through the land, long hikes in mountain trails and sprawling plains, and another on reinforcing himself and his magics. Eventually they found their Patron, one said to be the heart of a fallen giant of time beyond, the first of the motley bargained with his knowledge, the third on her persuasion, but the second made the deal, the mountain demanding consistency was impressed by him, constantly coming back when his companions failed, every time climbing the hike, in snow, in rain, in the scorching sun and relentless rains, to request protection and stability. Now Huntsmen and their masters must do the same, the Bargain with Horsetooth Mountain forcing the would be takers to slowly prepare, to slowly and carefully trudge through rugged terrain, with a singular target in mind, as the founder of the court had done so many decades before, and when the Others get there, the Court of Endurance will be ready, and they won\u2019t go back.<br /> The rituals of the Slate Circle are often subtle and simple, about the small things to be found in life, often taking routine hikes in the surrounding area, keeping up with a tight exercise regiment or local community charities, keeping their Patron mountain clean and healthy. When the work piles on and becomes too heavy, at the end of their time in the limelight of a Freehold, they host a grand feast, of alcohol and mortal foods, of goblin fruits and decadent deserts, let themselves go for just an evening, before they go back to work once more, singing honors of the lost and the mighty, of the hidden and the loud, this is the one chance to have a real break, and no deals or bargains are allowed to be made during this feast.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T01:05:27-07:00","id":1550206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rexitonic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1549589-custom-courts?p=1550205#post1550205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finished the Court of Stone second draft a while ago, though I regrettably took sleeping pills midway through and lost my path, so some bits are a bit spotty.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Finished the Court of Leaves just now as well! Both of these are in the doc under the second drafts section, with some preamble dedicated to my thoughts and process for them, this time I didn't take sleeping pills <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T20:27:32-07:00","id":1550295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rexitonic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1549589-custom-courts?p=1550206#post1550206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finished the Court of Leaves just now as well! Both of these are in the doc under the second drafts section, with some preamble dedicated to my thoughts and process for them, this time I didn't take sleeping pills <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think we may need a new link, because the document in the existing link does not have a second drafts section nor a preamble and its section on the Court of Stone does not match the second draft you've posted in-thread.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Stone second draft, the second half definitely wanders out of focus a bit, but it's closer now to having a story to its foundation. There's a little confusion I'm running into with the second member of the motley being the one to strike the deal, given that once a changeling has failed to strike a Bargain with a particular patron they can never try for it again, and it's probably worth giving some more attention to how the Court's activities evoke its patron rather than just their agreement with it.<br /> <br /> There may be something to be done with the Court's focus on reliability and their patron supposedly being the heart of a giant; I would perhaps frame it less as monotony than as that bit from The Man Who Was Thursday about how amazing it is for a train to go to the same stations in the same order every time in a chaotic universe, if only to have something for the &quot;changelings join this court when\u2026&quot; segment of a theoretical writeup \u2014 even the gloomier courts tend to have some sort of glamor to them, for all that sometimes it's just being able to brag about what your station requires you to go through. Part of me thinks there's metaphors to be had about a Court patronized by a giant's heart having rituals based in physical exercise (in the sense that a good exercise routine tends to lower the variance of one's heart rate), and the Wizened seeming curse has me wondering if the stories say anything about their founder having been a member of the stereotypically most diminutive seeming having sworn a Bargain with one of the biggest sorts of things in the natural world and/or a piece of a giant.<br /> <br /> I'd caution that &quot;They don't do stuff for free&quot; is another one of those &quot;That's every court, these are fae survivors with natural trust issues for which ostensibly selfless altruism tends to ring warning bells&quot; things; I would also add that while the release-valve feasts are kind of a staple of this general archetype of court, it seems out of keeping with this particular court's focuses to suspend the primary method of ensuring trustworthiness right before they pivot to keeping things running when they aren't in charge.<br /> <br /> Does the Bargain's effects on the Gentry geographically limit their pursuits to places the courtiers have to be anyway but are liable to be prepared for conflict?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T23:36:08-07:00","id":1550296,"title":"","content":"Oh I had no idea about the link! Thank you for alerting me, it's been updated. And thank you again for your attention I value your critism and comments a great deal <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll definitely be doing a third draft on the Court of Stone, I like the change from Monotony and I think I'll utilize what you mentioned, and in all honesty, I completely forgot that bit about not being able to attempt patronage again! It's been a while since I read the 2e supplements, I should find that section again.<br /> <br /> As for the last comment, it does not limit, the idea is more that it gives the Changelings themselves more time to prep, forcing the Gentry to go slowly. The person's original idea was (she doesn't have much experience with any of this, but neither do I tbh) the huntsmen or gentry would have to put on pure focus into capturing a single changeling and spend everyday working towards it (one thought she had was they'd have to constantly carry a rock with the targets name on it, if they loose it they have to start over or can't target them). So I'm trying to get the essence of what she wanted with that and put it towards something, a bit more useful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T21:01:16-07:00","id":1550330,"title":"","content":"Looking at the rest of the second drafts via the updated link, I will note that, like OA&amp;T says, the specific metaphysical category of a Court's non-abstract patron is ultimately fairly unimportant unless that branch of the metaphysics is relevant to its Bargain, as long as it isn't fae in nature (so it's a good thing nobody was particularly interested in the True Fae option \u2014 <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1495989-have-any-you-created-your-own-changeling-court?p=1496016#post1496016\">my own custom Courts</a>, created and partially developed before OA&amp;T came out, had to shift the focus of their patronage a degree or two of removal and still lean on some Contagion-adjacent weirdness, as the Great Star ostensibly <i>used to be</i> one of the Fae before its death left behind something markedly stranger and more volatile, and that theory largely stands on the fact that demons have been able to use it to specifically bridge their own pacts with the Wyrd).<br /> <br /> Reading the new Court of Leaves, it occurs to me that there could be some fun synergy in the patterns imposed by the Bargains of Stone and Leaves \u2014 perhaps forcing the Strangers to use methods that have and have not been tried before, respectively, with documentation of prior attempts being an evergreen role in the freehold (perhaps an entitlement?).<br /> <br /> It may be prudent, if framing the Courts as connected by their relation to the fallen giant, to approach those patrons as specifically dead/reborn remains of those pieces, particularly given that the description of Soot as grudge-holders taken in combination with their previous activities is kind of giving vengeful ghost vibes. Bearing that in mind, it might be good to reassign the Heart to the Court of Water and instead attribute Stone's Bargain to its Spine, or at least settle on what bits and types of anatomical symbolism you want to use. (Offhand I'd suggest Teeth or Gut for Soot and Throat or Voice for Leaves.)<br /> <br /> Especially if Underworld stuff ends up in-focus, you could do a lot worse than taking cues from the krewe Archetypes of Geist and transplanting their approaches to the dead onto the Courts' approaches to Change (in order, I'd match Undertakers, Mourners, Pilgrims, Necropolitans). It's not a perfect fit, particularly given that krewe Archetypes are all ostensibly geared at least partially toward effecting change and Stone's deal is counter-change, but looking at the Courts as goal-oriented groups may be useful at least in conceiving of ways a given changeling could be sold on joining them (as distinct from the collection of magical quirks attached to their coping mechanism).<br /> <br /> It might be good, in the course of filling out the local supernatural scene, to connect the Courts' patrons (and other pieces of the giant) to what Mage calls Mysteries and what OA&amp;T's Freehold Building tool refers to as Wonders \u2014 perhaps weird skeins of copper hair can be found twined around buried utility lines, or an irregularly-recurring living thunderstorm rumbles in an ancient language some of the freeholders recognize only from their durances, or the area around the Spine provides the benefit of one of its Contracts to anyone who fulfills the Loophole. It never hurts to have custom Courts be deeply entangled with local strangeness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}